$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Tables 1 and 3 A vial
was equipped with a magnetic stir bar and charged with precatalyst 13
(2-3 mol%) and the boronic acid (1.5 mmol). The vessel was sealed with a
screw-cap septum, and then evacuated and backfilled with argon (this
process was repeated a total of 3 times). Then, the aryl halide or pseudo
halide (1.0 mmol) and degassed THF (2 mL) were added via syringe (aryl
halides that were solids at room temperature were added with the
precatalyst and the boronic acid). Then, degassed 0.5 M aqueous K3PO4
solution (4 mL) was added via syringe and the reaction was stirred at
room temperature or 40 °C for 30 min or 2 h. At this point, diethyl ether
(10 mL) and water (10 mL) were added to the mixture, and the aqueous
phase was extracted with diethyl ether (3 × 10 mL). The organic phase was
dried over MgSO4, concentrated in vacuo, and purified via the Biotage SP4
(silica-packed 25g snap cartridge). 2-(benzo[b]thiophen-2-yl)quinoline
(21b).4 Following the general procedure, a mixture of 2-chloroquinoline
(164 mg, 1.0 mmol), boronic acid 6 (267 mg, 1.5 mmol), precatalyst 13
(15.7 mg, 2 mol%), degassed THF (2 mL) and degassed aqueous 0.5 M K3PO4
solution (4 mL) were stirred at 40 °C for 30 min. In contrast to the
general procedure, the aqueous workup required CH2Cl2 in place of Et2O
due to solubility reasons. The crude product was purified via the Biotage
SP4 (silica-packed 25 g snap column; 5-90% CH2Cl2/hexanes) to provide the
title compound as a colorless solid (240 mg, 92%). mp = 191-192 °C (lit:4
190 °C); 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.15 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 7.96 (s,
1H), 7.94 - 7.88 (m, 2H), 7.86 - 7.81 (m, 1H), 7.79 (dd, J = 8.1, 1.3 Hz,
1H), 7.73 (ddd, J = 8.4, 6.9, 1.4 Hz, 1H), 7.56 - 7.48 (m, 1H), 7.42 -
7.34 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ 152.31, 148.15, 145.55, 141.19,
140.48, 136.57, 129.96, 129.50, 127.54, 127.50, 126.56, 125.35, 124.54,
124.32, 122.64, 122.44, 117.81; IR (film) νmax 1594, 1500, 1427, 932,
827, 746, 729, 624 cm-1; Anal. Calcd. for C17H11NS: C, 78.13; H, 4.24.
Found: C, 78.15; H, 4.21.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki-Miyaura cross-coupling reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A New Palladium Precatalyst Allows for the Fast Suzuki-Miyaura Coupling
Reactions of Unstable Polyfluorophenyl and 2-Heteroaryl Boronic Acids
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Kinzel, Tom; Zhang, Yong; Buchwald, Stephen L.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2010), 132(40), 14073-14075

