$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-(Phenylsulfonyl)-4-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1H-pyrrolo[2,3-b]pyridine.
In a sealed tube were combined
4-bromo-1-(phenylsulfonyl)-1H-pyrrolo[2,3-b]pyridine (3.87 g, 11.48
mmol), potassium acetate (3.38 g, 34.43 mmol), bis(pinacolato) diboron
(3.50 g, 13.77 mmol), and 1,1'-bis(diphenylphosphino)
ferrocenepalladium(II)dichloride dichloromethane complex (0.375 g, 0.46
mmol) followed by anhydrous 1,4-dioxane (115 mL). The reaction mixture
was stirred at 100°C for 45 min and then cooled to room temperature.
After dilution with EtOAc (50 mL) and filtration through a pad of celite,
the filtrate was concentrated in vacuo. The residue was purified by
silica gel chromatography, eluting with 20-50% ethyl acetate/hexanes to
provide the title product as a white solid (4.06 g, 92%).
1-(Phenylsulfonyl)-4-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1H-pyrrolo[2,3-b]pyridine,
yield 4.06 g, 92%. MS m/z 384.0 [M + H]+. 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ ppm
1.32 (12H, s), 6.97 (1H, d, J = 4.04 Hz), 7.48 (1H, d, J = 4.80 Hz), 7.61
(2H, t, J = 7.71 Hz), 7.71 (1H, t, J = 7.45 Hz), 7.98 (1H, d, J = 4.04
Hz), 8.05-8.15 (2H, m), 8.38 (1H, d, J = 4.55 Hz).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM sealed tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of GSK1070916, a Potent and Selective Inhibitor of Aurora B/C
Kinase
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Adams, Nicholas D.; Adams, Jerry L.; Burgess, Joelle L.; Chaudhari, Amita
