$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Step 1: To a mixture of 2-bromo-N-methoxy-N-methyl-isonicotinamide (550
mg, 2.24 mmol), isoquinone-3-boromic acid (579 mg, 3.36 mmol, 1.5 equiv),
Pd2(dba)3 (6 mg, 0.03 equiv.) and S-Phos
(2-dicyclohexylphosphino-2',6'-dimethoxybiphenyl; 165 mg, 0.4 mmol, 0.18
equiv) were added dioxane (30 mL), water (0.3 mL) and K3PO4 (951 mg, 4.50
mmol, 2.0 equiv). The vessel was evacuated and flushed with N2 several
times to remove oxygen. The resulting mixture was heated at 120 °C for 40
min in a microwave reactor. The reaction mixture was then cooled and
concentrated. The residue was purified by silica gel column
chromatography (EtOAc/heptane 0 to 100%) to give
2-isoquinolin-4-yl-N-methoxy-N-methyl-isonicotinamide. Yield 605 mg, 92%.
1H NMR (400 MHz, CD2Cl2) δ 9.22 (s, 1 H), 8.80 (s, 1 H), 8.56 (s, 1 H),
8.16 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 1 H), 8.00 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1 H), 7.76 (s, 1 H), 7.71
- 7.55 (m, 2 H), 7.50 (d, J = 5.0 Hz, 1 H), 3.53 (s, 3 H), 3.28 (s, 3 H);
MS m/z 294.1 [M+H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Fragment-Based Discovery of 7-Azabenzimidazoles as Potent, Highly
Selective, and Orally Active CDK4/6 Inhibitors
