$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 7-tert-Butoxycarbonyl-2-exo-[2′ -amino-3′ -(2-fluoropyridin-4-yl)-5′
-pyridinyl]-7-azabicyclo[2.2.1]heptane (12b). A solution of compound 9
(319 mg, 0.87 mmol, 1.0 equiv), 2-fluoropyridine-4- boronic acid (196 mg,
1.39 mmol, 1.6 equiv), Pd(OAc)2 (20 mg, 0.087 mmol, 10 mol %),
P(o-tolyl)3 (53 mg, 0.173 mmol, 20 mol %), and Na2CO3 (184 mg, 1.73 mmol,
2.0 equiv) in DME (6 mL) and water (0.7 mL) was degassed through bubbling
nitrogen for 20 min. The mixture was sealed and heated over a sand bath
at 80 °C for 5 h. After cooling to room temperature, the mixture was
poured into a saturated aqueous solution of NaHCO3 (20 mL) and extracted
with EtOAc (3 × 30 mL). The combined organic layers were dried over
MgSO4, filtered through Celite, and concentrated in vacuo. The resultant
residue was purified by flash chromatography on silica gel using
EtOAc-hexanes as the eluent to provide 12b. Colorless oil, yield 300 mg,
92%. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.4 (br s, 9H), 1.52-1.59 (m, 2H),
1.82-1.84 (m, 3H), 1.94-1.98 (m, 1H), 2.79-2.84 (m, 1H), 4.16 (s, 1H),
4.36 (br s, 1H), 4.77 (s, 2 NH), 7.06 (s, 1H), 7.34 (ddd, J= 1.6, 5.13,
8.4 Hz, 1H), 7.41 (d, J= 2.3 Hz, 1H), 8.0 (d, J= 2.3 Hz, 1H), 8.26 (d, J=
5.16 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 28.3 (3 C), 28.8, 29.7, 40.5, 44.8, 55.9,
62.1, 79.7, 108.8, 121.1, 132.5, 136.5, 147.8, 148.3, 152.0, 153.7,
155.0, 162.8, 166.0. MS (ESI) m/z 385.3 (M + H)+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling, sealed tube used
