$DATUM 4-(2-Fluoropyridin-3-yl)-N,N-bis(4-methoxybenzyl)-6-methyl-1,3,5-triazin-2-amine
(71f). A mixture of 66 (1.57 g, 4.08 mmol), 2-fluoropyridin-3-ylboronic
acid (632 mg, 4.48 mmol), Pd(Amphos)2Cl2 (144 mg, 0.20 mmol), and KOAc
(1.22 g, 12.4 mmol) in EtOH (15 mL) and H2O (1.5 mL) contained in a 20 mL
microwave tube was degassed by bubbling Ar through it for 5 min. The
mixture was heated in a microwave reactor at 100 °C for 20 min. The
reaction mixture was partitioned between a 1:1 mixture of H2O and
saturated brine (150 mL) and EtOAc (50 mL). The aqueous phase was
extracted with EtOAc (50 mL). The combined organic phases were washed
with saturated brine (50 mL). The organic phase was dried (Na2SO4),
filtered, concentrated, and purified by silica gel column chromatography
(gradient: 10% → 50% EtOAc/hexanes) to give 71f. Yield (1.65 g, 91%),
pale-yellow oil. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.62-8.49 (m, 1H), 7.99-7.86
(m, 1H), 7.36-7.27 (m, 1H), 7.23 (dd, J = 8.31, 4.99 Hz, 4H), 6.87 (t, J
= 8.51 Hz, 4H), 3.81 (s, 3H), 4.81 (s, 4H), 3.80 (s, 3H), 2.55 (s, 3H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Structure-Based Design of a Novel Series of Potent, Selective Inhibitors
of the Class I Phosphatidylinositol 3-Kinases
