$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General synthesis of NP oligomers by Suzuki coupling
Dibromo-oligo(N-annulated perylenes) 2, 6, 8, 12 (1.0 mmol) and NP
monoboronic ester 4 (3.0 mmol), Pd(PPh3)4 (0.10 mmol) and Cs2CO3 (10
mmol) were added into three-neck bottle under argon. Then degassed
toluene (50 mL) and DMF (2 mL) were added and purged with argon. The
mixture was stirred at 90 °C for 36 hours. After reaction completed and
cooled to room temperature, water was added. The product was extracted
with ethyl acetate (3 x 100 mL). The organic layer was washed with
saturated brine and dried over anhydrous Na2SO4. The solvent was removed
under vacuum and the residue was dissolved in minimum amount of DCM (1.5
mL). The solution in DCM was then added dropwise into methanol (100 mL).
The excess oily boronic ester 4 could be washed with a large amount of
methanol while the desired compounds showed poor solubility in methanol.
The precipitate was collected by filtration and further washed with
methanol to afford the pure product as yellow solids. Compound 7 Yellow
solid; 90% yield. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 500 MHz): δ 8.82-8.78 (m, 8H), 8.26-8.19
(m, 4H), 8.16-8.04 (m, 4H), 8.04-7.93 (m, 2H), 7.78-7.29 (m, 10H),
7.75-7.67 (m, 6H), 4.71-4.66 (m, 8H), 2.40-2.38 (m, 4H), 1.44 (m, 20H),
1.21-1.05 (m, 140H), 0.88-0.78 (m, 24H). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 75 MHz): δ
136.58, 132.42, 132.35, 132.23, 130.76, 130.59, 129.61, 129.50, 129.47,
128.91, 124.99, 124.92, 124.58, 124.52, 123.75, 120.94, 120.88, 120.82,
117.70, 117.39, 117.15, 115.81, 115.73, 115.62, 113.73, 50.47, 50.26,
40.10, 40.08, 31.91, 31.88, 31.83, 29.98, 29.94, 29.70, 29.59, 29.55,
29.33, 29.28, 29.24, 26.53, 26.64, 22.59, 14.10. HRMS (MALDI-TOF, m/z):
caldc for C176H230N4, 2399.8115; found, 2399.8182 (error = + 2.8 ppm).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Pushing Extended p-Quinodimethanes to the Limit: Stable
Tetracyano-oligo(N-annulated perylene)quinodimethanes with Tunable Ground
States
