$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 3-amino-N,6-diphenylpyrazine-2-carboxamide
(6). Method A: General Procedure for Suzuki Cross-Coupling; Compounds 6,
11-33, 35, and 39-41. To reaction tubes containing
3-amino-6-bromo-N-phenyl-pyrazine-2-carboxamide 8 (88 mg, 0.3 mmol) in
DMF (4 mL) were added boronic acid or ester (0.3 mmol) followed by
Pd(PPh3)2Cl2 or Pd(PPh3)4 (5 mol %) and 2 M aqueous Na2CO3 solution (2
mL). The tubes were then flushed with N2 and heated to 88 °C for 18 h.
After this time, the reactions were allowed to cool to ambient
temperature, filtered, and purified by reverse phase HPLC to give the
desired products as solids after lyophilization (yields ranged from 10 to
90%). Analytical data for 6, 11-33, 35, and 39-41 are provided in the
Supporting Information. 3-amino-N,6-diphenylpyrazine-2-carboxamide (6).
3-amino-N-phenyl-6-(pyridin-4-yl)pyrazine-2-carboxamide (12). Prepared
according to Method A; yellow solid. MS (ES+) m/z 292 (M + H)+; 1H NMR
(400 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 10.48 (s, 1H), 9.07 (s, 1H), 8.67 (dd, 2H), 8.25
(dd, 2H), 7.90 (s, 2H), 7.82 (dd, 2H), 7.41 (dd, 2H) and 7.18 (t, 1H)
ppm; HRMS (ES+) calcd for C16H14N5O (M + H)+ 292.1198; found: 292.1227.
Retention time (min): 8.70; Purity: 100%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative reactant and catalyst may also be used (boronic ester,
Pd(Pph3)4), Suzuki cross- coupling reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of Potent and Selective Inhibitors of Ataxia Telangiectasia
Mutated and Rad3 Related (ATR) Protein Kinase as Potential Anticancer
Agents
